    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6a2823ebbc8f4ec2b70796d560761611",
      "statement": "`GitHubService` exposes exactly two write operations — post an issue comment and close an issue with state reason `Not_planned` — and no label, pull request, review, or merge operation, which makes the PRD's label transitions and PR creation stages unimplemented rather than mis-wired.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/GitHub/GitHubService.cs#L40-L69",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0d35813228612814134624f4040cb51d61aac022ec123b62b02fe07731be9c3d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8bf525524ba64968888cb794971fe568",
      "statement": "The git layer cannot publish: `Git` offers fetch, `merge --ff-only`, worktree add/prune, status, rev-parse, rev-list, remote get-url, and branch --show-current, with no commit, push, or PR primitive, and the agent shell deny-list blocks `git push|reset|clean|checkout --` and `gh` but does not block `git commit`, so \"no commit\" is prompt-enforced while \"no publish\" is denial-enforced.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/Roles/ImplementationAgent.cs#L55-L65",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5049ed3bbb0aa4dd41012e086287ad4453083a31676810c673c11db2e8b69745:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Libs/Git.cs#L79-L93",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ed5e9efb9797c7a6d183e9a6ec81cfe2b8805b1491f6bbaaf99b8ff740c8e0b7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ee4c7d4973204efabef4d01ab4c175c3",
      "statement": "The implementation prompt tells the agent to treat the issue body as requirements, not add dependencies, not touch files outside the workspace, not run git/commit/push/create PRs, and to stop if the spec is ambiguous; the host verifies none of this afterwards and a successful run ends at a completion log containing the worktree path, short git status, and agent response text.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L112-L135",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c85571a8ba32b1f7e032fbdd337cfc9bda85aba0246845878060389e5ecbd15b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/ImplementSpec.cs#L50-L51",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:32d5e46dd9e3d1c117e051c9962cec18c472fd08dbb9c983b249cbbdd358b720:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_68cd767133cf4d50a0a4520cad182cc7",
      "statement": "The agent sandbox is the only guard at execution time: a `LocalShellExecutor` confined to the worktree with a scrubbed environment, a ten-minute command timeout, and a deny-list of destructive/network/git-publishing patterns, run with approvals disabled and execute mode — which also means a hostile issue body cannot read credentials from the agent's shell environment, the code-level answer to the PRD's prompt-injection risk.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/Roles/ImplementationAgent.cs#L21-L72",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:85acf3228527072ecf2fae90b01191ec0e6b868744d725091ce4723b7a27e2ca:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Agent/Roles/ImplementationAgent.cs#L25-L42",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c346db72a1957c10bb46d148e1ccb9d0c092047f0cd98e1c1c5838079e156826:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7dfb311d8eb84dba9baae9853ccc934b",
      "statement": "Configuration carries no cost, budget, or rate-limit surface: `SebastianConfig` has only `GitHub` and `Agent` sections, and the agent section holds provider name, endpoint, api key, and model id, so the PRD's per-run and per-day cost ceilings have no code behind them.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Configuration/SebastianConfig.cs#L9-L67",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:03e295679fffe161fa5079a88fd4bdc92ca0ec0575eb4ba26c7c4f626514140e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_52d1680e26e34d3bbe5ee35a8917e969",
      "statement": "Only `IssuesEvent` and `PushEvent` are routed by the webhook processor; push deliveries synchronously call `Git.SyncMainAsync` inside the request, and every other event type — including pull request and issue comment events, which is where a `merge` command would have to arrive — falls through to the base processor and does nothing.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/Webhooks/GitHubWebhookProcessor.cs#L107-L117",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:157fae54eb39a767fcaa9562bc592d1cfa5a6be5dadf7c984f9a08e5a9cc7400:"
